        "t": "text",
        "v": " Precision asks: of the items flagged positive, how many were right? Recall asks: of the real positives, how many did we catch? F1 is their harmonic mean, so it punishes a model that is strong on one and weak on the other. The doc's sentiment example uses F1 for exactly this reason. Use precision and recall separately when the two error types have different costs, such as fraud detection where a missed case costs more than a false alarm. [1][7]"
