     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "The middle row is an easy yes: an 80% cut on the subagent share, and the pass-rate loss does not erase it. The third row is the same design with a harder task distribution, and it is now more expensive per completed run than the all-Opus baseline. The break-even is $1.76 ÷ $4.35 ≈ 40%: below that pass rate, the cheap subagents lose. This is the calculation an architect owes a stakeholder, and it is why the docs put \"low effort, subagent tasks\" in Haiku's column only after your evals confirm quality holds. [3][8][14]"
       }
      ]
     }
