     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "How to alert on the cache."
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " Share, not absolute count. Cached tokens rise and fall with traffic, so an absolute threshold pages you every Monday morning. "
       },
       {
        "t": "code",
        "v": "cache_read / (cache_read + cache_creation + input)"
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " is stable against volume and moves sharply when the prefix breaks. Confirm a suspected break in the Console's rate-limit and caching chart, which plots cache percentage hourly against your ITPM limit. [1][6][7]"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Online evaluation for quality."
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " Score production traces automatically as they are logged, asynchronously, so there is no latency cost. There is no ground truth for live requests, so this means an LLM judge rather than an exact-match grader. Pull the flagged traces into your offline dataset: that closes the loop, turning a production surprise into a permanent regression test. [5]"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Where it goes wrong."
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " Alerting on raw daily spend. Traffic doubles for a legitimate reason, the alert fires, someone silences it, and the real regression two weeks later fires into a muted channel. Normalize by completed tasks."
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "t": "p",
      "v": [
       {
        "t": "strong",
        "v": "Example."
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " A team sets a cache-share alert at 15 points below the 7-day baseline. A deploy adds a per-request timestamp to the top of the system prompt. The share falls from 91% to 4% within ten minutes, the alert fires, and the fix — move "
       },
       {
        "t": "code",
        "v": "cache_control"
       },
       {
        "t": "text",
        "v": " to the last block that is identical across requests — ships the same afternoon. Without the alert this surfaces on next month's invoice."
       }
      ]
     }
