        "t": "text",
        "v": " Anthropic's own practice on the multi-agent research system was high-level observability of agent decision patterns and interaction structures without accessing conversation content, precisely to preserve user privacy. That is the design an architect defends in a review: tool-call sequences, step counts, durations, and end states answer nearly every operational question, and reading conversations answers a few more at a cost most organizations should not pay by default. [4]"
